diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index e0ab1db93..c1f343488 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,13 @@ Entries are generated from [Changes](Changes/README.md). Existing release notes
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Repair remaining hosted runtime regressions with unchanged acceptance gates.
+  - Preserve viewer/Terminal kind across deferred unload and let enabled instance creation retry the safe unload sweep after the last old owner retires; retain busy refusal while an old owner remains.
+  - Keep viewer harness children console-free with restricted, bounded stdout/stderr capture and exact stream witnesses. Observe an already restored cross-thread child focus independently from permission to write restoration state, and retire ViewerWeb callbacks through the production unload gate.
+  - Make optional-backend VLC HUD keyboard coverage deterministic while retaining its real focus and available-backend playback checks.
+  - Reserve bounded Local provider worker capacity for competing jobs and give every scheduler stream its own state. Preserve the independent-volume byte, overlap and timing gates; resolve only validated test-owned VHDX child operation paths.
+  - Serialize every FTP fixture listing row with the same wire bytes and bounded decimal sizes, retaining all 142 original checks and adding a maximum-size oracle. Keep all wide-directory, transfer, ownership and deadline gates.
+  - Pin the documentation Terminal through its normal unopened factory before probing exports, drain and resample the final warm-quiescence boundary with an independent late-paint control, and report Find-sort snapshots after their actual waits. Native and hosted qualification remains pending.
 - Isolate captured console children from interactive consoles and their parent's console-control lifetime while retaining suspended Job assignment, bounded independent stream capture, deadlines and descendant containment. Strengthen the existing native child-process contract with an actual console-state probe and retain duplicate search-service exit/output diagnostics. The original helper fails the new console check; Debug and ASan each pass ten repetitions of all three focused runner/writer cases (30 checks per profile). Broader local and hosted runtime qualification remains pending.
 - Hold the notified test hotkey through its foreground handoff, then release it with scoped failure cleanup; keep the 500 ms bound and every ownership, focus and registration check. An independent native dispatch witness rejects the original early release. Preserve the failed control and the ten-pass ASan durable-store repetition receipt; current hosted qualification remains required.
 - Isolate every durable-store mechanics invocation in a fresh owned child directory, preserving prior fixture evidence and every immediate cleanup, retained-reader, reparse, limit and concurrency assertion. Keep read-only native case inventory outside the desktop lease while retaining admission and restoration for actual UI tests; focused regression controls verify both routes. Broader native qualification remains pending.
